  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"A diverse collection of art and artifacts created in response to the attack on artists and other groups by Senator Helms and his supporters. Works by local artists, documentation from around the country, posters, photographs, and written statements all deal with freedom of expression issues and various social questions brough to attention by extreme conservative factions"</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Catalog of the exhibition Extremely visible in protest of Senator Jesse Helms's attack on the National Endowment for the Arts. Held in 1990 at Seventh Street Restaurant &amp; Bar, Durham, NC, October 26-November 1; Hardback Cafe, Chapel Hill, November 2-8; Carolina Union Gallery, UNC Chapel Hill, November 7-17.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Artists: Cyrstal Cawley, Increase Maready, Rosie Thompson, Hunter Levinsohn, Anne Rowles, Brian Kennedy, Heidi Zednik, Anne Woodson, Ellen Hill, Beth Grabowski, Jennifer Haithcock, Xavier Toubes, Gina Gilmour, Denis Wood, Sarah Wilkins, Vernon Pratt.</subfield>
  </datafield>
